From c853b3c3f9ef72252fc93e231d14762dd7359efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:17:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/36] The studio level, in the panel: three levels, the
 chain, the stack, the plot

The parameters column now reads the capability descriptor instead of a
hand-written visibility table, so every control says which of the three
possible reasons refuses it and says it in the text rather than in a tooltip
nobody hovers.

New in the panel: the level switcher remembered per project, resolution
buckets per family with an off-bucket warning, the working point applied on
model switch with its reason and an undo, the pass chain as an editable list
with the denoise band drawn, the LoRA stack with trigger words, batch seed
mode, the prompt craft bar (weights, token estimate, wildcard picks and the
two A1111 tricks this runtime does not implement), and the X/Y/Z plot.
